## Best Practices (2025)

1. **Use AI agents for exploration** - Let Planner agent discover test scenarios
2. **Auto-generate assertions** - Enable in Codegen for toBeVisible() checks
3. **Leverage healer agent** - Auto-repair flaky tests
4. **Use role-based selectors** - More maintainable than CSS selectors
5. **Reuse authentication state** - Don't login in every test
6. **Mock external APIs** - Fast, reliable, isolated tests
7. **Enable trace on failures** - Easy debugging with Trace Viewer
8. **Parallel execution** - Faster test suite completion
9. **Block unnecessary resources** - Images, fonts for speed
10. **Page Object Model** - Encapsulate page interactions
11. **Auto-wait is built-in** - No manual waits needed
12. **Test across browsers** - Use project configuration
13. **Visual regression** - Catch UI changes
14. **CI integration** - Use reporters (HTML, JSON, JUnit)
15. **Keep tests independent** - Each test should work in isolation
